No direct answer, but something to consider:  if you are getting
headaches from eyestrain, your vision may not be properly corrected
even though the fonts seem readable (perhaps slight astigmatism?).
That, or the monitor may not be in focus.  

My vision is corrected from 20/700 to 20/15 with my contact lenses,
and I use fonts that make everyone else in the office squint.  I
haven't noticed the screen being more difficult to read with my
glasses (which can only correct to about 20/20), but I do know I have
a slightly harder time with street signs and other faraway objects.

